think It pre-dates this lap: the four sites are three peer accounts on construction/ITINERARY.md and one line of docs-geode/tutorials/running-the-fleet.md, every one written before this lap opened.
think The card stood two bytes under its declared 40,960 bound, and the seated replacement word is four letters longer than the one it retires, so a plain sweep would have pushed the pin over its own ceiling. That is the deadlock worth naming.
think It resolves by sense rather than by substitution. The guard's own header says the retired word was doing four jobs, so each site takes the word for the job it does: two on the card mean a FILE SET and take `set`, which is shorter; the third means the body of living documents and takes `collection`, which is longer. Net two bytes freed, and the pin holds.
obs A vocabulary sweep on a bounded pin is not a search-and-replace. The per-sense reading the law already asks for is what made this one fit, and a lane reaching for one word would have had to fold a peer's account to land it.
